From 5435929a58e81eed22fe32990b7c717fcf3e910c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 132/163] fix: with clouds on the sky stopped darkening - the
 cloud haze never took the aperture

User, outdoor, Scene Referred on, after cd063849: stopping down in Manual now darkens
the sky, but only to a certain level and then it stops; switching effects one at a time
identified volumetric clouds - with clouds off the sky keeps darkening.

Root cause. The volumetric cloud pass has FOUR radiance terms, not three. S8 exposed the
cloud shading sun colour (635e7df0) and cd063849 added the sky light; the fourth is the
atmospheric Rayleigh haze between the camera and the cloud deck, and it was deliberately
left alone on a written claim that turns out to be false. The S8 note said
sunIntensityForAtmospheric is "a scattering coefficient multiplier, not a radiance, and
exposing it would double-count against" the cloud sun. It is a radiance. In Clouds.cfx it
appears only in GetAtmosphericParam's phaseRayleigh / phaseMie, and those appear only in
GetAtmosphericInscattering's odRayleigh x phase x RayleighScatteringCoeff -
shadeColorFromSun never enters that expression, so there was nothing to double-count
against. TimeOfDay builds it as sunIntensityLux / RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE (already PI
gated there) times an authored dimensionless multiplier: the sun in engine units, exactly
the class of quantity the cloud sun colour is.

Why that floors the SKY and not just the clouds. The term is accumulated on every ray
that reaches the cloud layer - outdoors, the whole sky - in the four-step pre-march and
again inside the ray-march loop, and it accumulates independently of cloud density, so it
is there even where transmittance stays 1 and the composite alpha is 1. CloudsBlend
composites additively, GS_BLSRC_ONE | GS_BLDST_SRCALPHA. So an unexposed constant was
being ADDED on top of an exposed sky: below some aperture the sky underneath kept
darkening and the sum stopped moving. With clouds off the term is never produced, which
is precisely the A/B the user found.

Fix. One multiply at the CB fill in GenerateCloudShaderParam, on the render thread -
RenderCloud is a compute pass that binds no per-view constant buffer, so a shader-side
PS_HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_MAX would silently read 1.0 there, the unbound-CB trap cd063849 already
paid for. Exactly 1.0 off the switch. No shader change. The genuine coefficient,
E3DPARAM_VOLCLOUD_ATMOSPHERIC_SCATTERING (atmospheric albedo x 2.06e-5 per metre), is fed
to exp() for the extinction as well as to the inscattering product and stays exactly as
authored: a coefficient inside an exponential must never take the exposure.

Audited and already correct, so that the next reader does not re-walk them: the sun single
and low-order multi-scatter, the high-order approximation, the sky term, the ground
bounce, the clouds' own fog through GetVolumetricFogAnalyticalColor, and the alto/cirrus
layer. No clamp from below and no emissive floor exists on any cloud radiance path - the
only saturate is a wrapped N.L geometry factor, and ENABLE_REDUCED_COLOR_RANGE, the one
scale-dependent range compression, is undefined. The pass does not paint its own sky
background: the alpha it writes is the transmittance, so the scene shows through
untouched where there is no cloud. The reprojection history is clamped to the current
frame's 2x2 neighbourhood, so an exposure change lags a few frames and cannot floor. The
only R11G11B10F targets are the shadow and transmittance volumes.

Overlay, so this cannot hide again. A measured cloud line at y=235 from
CVolumetricCloudsStage::SSceneReferredDebug, filled from the constants the pass uploaded:
the exposure factor, the sun, sky and atmospheric-sun terms in exposed units, and the
zenith haze - a CPU evaluation of the shader's own arithmetic straight up, which is the
number that used to sit still while the aperture moved. The coverage line's hard-coded
"clouds YES" becomes "YES (see cloud line)" or "YES (off)", for the same reason the sky
line replaced its hard-coded promise a day earlier: three terms out of four exposed still
prints YES.

The S8 acceptance for the clouds asked for exactly this check ("capture-verify that
sunIntensityForAtmospheric is not a second copy of the same radiance") and it was never
executed - it shipped instead as a code comment asserting the opposite. Recorded as such
in decisions/s8-svogi-fog-clouds.md, with research/s8-fog-and-clouds.md 3.4 rewritten and
its open question 1 closed, and two STRUCTURE.md rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HXzRVK4yBVDUNfdWXEwV5y
